1
00:00:00,751 --> 00:00:01,919
Okay, the reason why

2
00:00:01,961 --> 00:00:03,211
I asked you guys out
to brunch today is

3
00:00:03,253 --> 00:00:04,797
because I've been doing
some thinking

4
00:00:04,839 --> 00:00:06,590
about who should be
my Maid of Honor.

5
00:00:06,632 --> 00:00:08,425
Oh, my God,
this is it!

6
00:00:08,467 --> 00:00:09,468
Oh!

7
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:10,886
I really hope it's you.

8
00:00:10,928 --> 00:00:11,804
I hope it's you.

9
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:12,972
Me, too.

10
00:00:14,306 --> 00:00:16,600
First of all, I love you both
so much

11
00:00:16,642 --> 00:00:18,978
and you're both so important
to me...

12
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:21,062
Okay, blah-la-la-la.
Who is it?

13
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:23,398
Well, I was thinking that

14
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,900
maybe we could come up
with a system

15
00:00:24,942 --> 00:00:27,152
where we trade off being
Maid of Honor for each other.

16
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:29,029
Like, hypothetically,
if Phoebe were mine...

17
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:30,656
Yes! Oh!

18
00:00:30,698 --> 00:00:33,742
Hypothetically.

19
00:00:33,784 --> 00:00:35,076
Still.

20
00:00:36,912 --> 00:00:39,373
If Phoebe were my Maid of Honor,
Rachel would be Phoebe's.

21
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:41,124
I would be Rachel's.

22
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:43,293
That way we all get to do it
once and no one would get upset.

23
00:00:43,335 --> 00:00:45,754
Uh-hmm. No, that's
actually a pretty good idea.

24
00:00:45,796 --> 00:00:46,755
Yeah, I'll do that.

25
00:00:46,797 --> 00:00:47,798
So, who gets to be yours?

26
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:50,467
Well, this is the best part.

27
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:52,720
You guys get to decide.

28
00:00:52,761 --> 00:00:56,390
Why is that
the best part?

29
00:00:56,431 --> 00:00:57,933
Because then I don't have to.

30
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:01,562
Well, of course
we will help you decide.

31
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:03,898
We will do anything
we can to help you.

32
00:01:03,939 --> 00:01:06,066
Okay, now, I'd like
to make a toast:

33
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:09,319
To the future Mrs. Chandler Bing

34
00:01:09,361 --> 00:01:11,446
my best friend

35
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:13,490
and truly one
of the nicest people that...

36
00:01:13,532 --> 00:01:15,576
Really not deciding.

37
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:16,368
Fine!

38
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:17,369
Excuse me.

39
00:01:17,411 --> 00:01:19,872
I couldn't help
overhearing.

40
00:01:19,914 --> 00:01:22,583
You're marrying Chandler Bing?

41
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:23,584
Yeah, that's right.

42
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:24,835
Huh...

43
00:01:24,877 --> 00:01:26,211
Good luck!

44
00:01:27,671 --> 00:01:30,674
Oh, and good luck to you, too.

45
00:01:30,716 --> 00:01:32,676
What a nice lady.

46
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:43,812
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

47
00:01:43,854 --> 00:01:45,856
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

48
00:01:45,898 --> 00:01:48,984
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

49
00:01:49,026 --> 00:01:53,697
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

50
00:01:53,739 --> 00:01:55,866
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

51
00:01:55,908 --> 00:01:59,327
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

52
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:03,331
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

53
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:08,754
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

54
00:02:13,425 --> 00:02:14,551
Both:
Yeah!
Woo-hoo!

55
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:16,887
Die Hard--
still great.

56
00:02:16,929 --> 00:02:19,014
Yup.

57
00:02:19,056 --> 00:02:21,892
Hey, what do you say
we make it a double feature?

58
00:02:21,934 --> 00:02:23,018
What else
did you rent?

59
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:25,562
Die Hard II!

60
00:02:25,604 --> 00:02:28,523
Joey, this is
Die Hard I again.

61
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:30,901
Oh...

62
00:02:30,943 --> 00:02:32,694
Well, we watch it
a second time

63
00:02:32,736 --> 00:02:33,988
and it's Die Hard II!

64
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,740
Joey, we just saw it.

65
00:02:36,782 --> 00:02:38,033
And?

66
00:02:38,075 --> 00:02:40,577
And it would be cool
to see it again. Yeah!

67
00:02:40,619 --> 00:02:42,788
Both:
Die Hard!

68
00:02:44,289 --> 00:02:47,167
Dude, you didn't say "Die Hard."

69
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:49,377
Is everything okay?

70
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:51,880
Yeah, I just got,
uh, I got plans.

71
00:02:51,922 --> 00:02:55,926
Well, John McClain had plans.

72
00:02:55,968 --> 00:02:58,595
No, you see, the thing is,
I want to get out of here

73
00:02:58,637 --> 00:03:00,139
before Joey gets all worked up

74
00:03:00,179 --> 00:03:01,932
and starts calling
everybody "bitch."

75
00:03:01,974 --> 00:03:06,103
What are you talking
about, bitch?

76
00:03:08,022 --> 00:03:09,731
Yeah?
Hey, Rachel.

77
00:03:09,773 --> 00:03:14,444
When I get married,
will you be my Maid of Honor?

78
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:15,696
Really?

79
00:03:15,737 --> 00:03:19,783
Oh, my God, Phoebe.
I mean, I'm just...

80
00:03:19,825 --> 00:03:21,451
Wait a minute.

81
00:03:21,493 --> 00:03:24,454
If I'm your
Maid of Honor

82
00:03:24,496 --> 00:03:28,207
that means that
you are Monica's.

83
00:03:28,249 --> 00:03:30,961
Oh...

84
00:03:31,003 --> 00:03:32,420
Well, if that's what you want.

85
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:34,089
Oh!

86
00:03:34,131 --> 00:03:35,423
No! Wait, Phoebe.

87
00:03:35,465 --> 00:03:37,216
I want to be Monica's.

88
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:38,969
But why does it even matter?

89
00:03:39,011 --> 00:03:40,679
Why does it matter
so much to you?

90
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:43,473
Because this one is now!

91
00:03:43,515 --> 00:03:45,809
And, and it's two
of our best friends.

92
00:03:45,851 --> 00:03:48,187
Who knows what
you're going to marry?

93
00:03:50,689 --> 00:03:53,192
What, what if I marry Ross?

94
00:03:53,232 --> 00:03:54,193
Or Joey?

95
00:03:54,233 --> 00:03:55,276
( gasps )

96
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:56,319
You wouldn't.

97
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,032
Okay, look, Rachel

98
00:04:00,074 --> 00:04:02,409
I know you really want
to do this

99
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:04,786
but I've never been
Maid of Honor

100
00:04:04,828 --> 00:04:06,080
to anyone before

101
00:04:06,121 --> 00:04:08,916
and I know you've done it
at least twice.

102
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:10,333
Yeah, but, Phoebe...

103
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:13,837
Please, oh, please,
let me finish.

104
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:16,006
Oh, I guess that was it.

105
00:04:16,048 --> 00:04:18,926
Okay.

106
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:21,011
Okay, since you've
never done it before

107
00:04:21,053 --> 00:04:22,888
you can be
Monica's Maid of Honor.

108
00:04:22,930 --> 00:04:25,099
Oh, thank you so much!

109
00:04:26,183 --> 00:04:27,809
Yay.

110
00:04:27,851 --> 00:04:30,520
( sighs )

111
00:04:30,562 --> 00:04:32,106
I'm going to marry
someone good, you know.

112
00:04:33,774 --> 00:04:34,775
Oh, I know.

113
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:35,692
Better than Chandler.

114
00:04:35,734 --> 00:04:37,402
( scoffs )

115
00:04:53,043 --> 00:04:54,169
( both scream )

116
00:04:57,256 --> 00:04:58,132
What happened?!

117
00:04:58,173 --> 00:04:59,549
I don't know.

118
00:04:59,591 --> 00:05:02,677
We fell asleep, that is all.

119
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:06,056
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

120
00:05:06,098 --> 00:05:07,766
All right.

121
00:05:07,808 --> 00:05:09,059
Well, uh, I better go.

122
00:05:09,101 --> 00:05:10,351
Yeah, I think
that would be best.

123
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,104
Yeah, all right.
I'll talk to you later.

124
00:05:12,146 --> 00:05:13,105
Okay.

125
00:05:13,147 --> 00:05:14,648
But not about this.

126
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:15,649
No, never!

127
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:16,733
Never!

128
00:05:16,775 --> 00:05:19,402
So, uh...

129
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:20,654
Bye.

130
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:21,655
No touch! No touch!

131
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:22,697
No.

132
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,703
Hey, you know, a weird thing
happened today

133
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:30,205
when I was at brunch.

134
00:05:30,247 --> 00:05:32,082
This woman overheard that
I was marrying you

135
00:05:32,124 --> 00:05:33,416
and she wished me
good luck.

136
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:34,918
That's sweet.

137
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:38,088
No, it was more
like a "good luck!"

138
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:41,675
So, uh, what did
this woman look like?

139
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:44,178
She was, like, 30,
dark hair, attractive.

140
00:05:44,219 --> 00:05:46,513
Well, is there any chance
you were looking

141
00:05:46,554 --> 00:05:48,932
into a bright, shiny thing
called a mirror?

142
00:05:48,974 --> 00:05:50,184
Come on.

143
00:05:50,225 --> 00:05:51,643
Was it someone
you dated in college?

144
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:55,189
No, no, I only dated two girls
in college

145
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:57,649
both blonde,
both not attractive...

146
00:05:57,691 --> 00:05:58,817
Hold on one second.

147
00:05:58,859 --> 00:06:00,359
Let me check this out.

148
00:06:00,401 --> 00:06:01,486
What are you doing?

149
00:06:01,528 --> 00:06:03,488
Well, let's see.

150
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:06,283
Okay, uh, is that her?

151
00:06:06,325 --> 00:06:07,826
Oh, my God, yes!

152
00:06:07,868 --> 00:06:08,952
Who is she?

153
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:12,122
Julie Graff,
my camp girlfriend.

154
00:06:12,164 --> 00:06:13,874
Did you break up with her?

155
00:06:13,915 --> 00:06:17,376
No, we're still together.

156
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:20,130
( chuckles )

157
00:06:20,172 --> 00:06:22,549
Yeah, we went out
for two summers

158
00:06:22,590 --> 00:06:24,676
and then I broke
up with her.

159
00:06:24,718 --> 00:06:26,011
Why?

160
00:06:26,053 --> 00:06:28,347
Well, because she came
back the third summer

161
00:06:28,387 --> 00:06:31,141
and she had gotten
really fa...aaaa...aaaa...

162
00:06:34,061 --> 00:06:34,728
Fat?

163
00:06:34,769 --> 00:06:36,813
I did not say fat.

164
00:06:36,855 --> 00:06:40,108
I said fa...aaaa...aaaa...

165
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:43,528
You broke up with a girl
because she was fat?

166
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:47,657
Yeah, yeah, but it was
a really, really

167
00:06:47,699 --> 00:06:48,658
long time ago.

168
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,035
Does she still feel bad?

169
00:06:50,077 --> 00:06:51,661
Apparently, she does.

170
00:06:51,703 --> 00:06:55,040
Well, you know what they say,
elephants never forget.

171
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:01,380
Seriously,
good luck marrying me.

172
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:07,344
Hey, what's going on?

173
00:07:07,386 --> 00:07:09,054
Hey, Phoebe is going to be
Monica's Maid of Honor.

174
00:07:09,096 --> 00:07:10,597
Hey, well I hope
it goes better

175
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:12,057
than the last time
you did it

176
00:07:12,099 --> 00:07:13,892
for that girl
downstairs, remember?

177
00:07:13,934 --> 00:07:15,727
What? Hey!

178
00:07:15,769 --> 00:07:18,563
You have been
Maid of Honor before?

179
00:07:18,605 --> 00:07:23,151
You see, this is exactly why
you shouldn't lie.

180
00:07:23,193 --> 00:07:24,319
All right, that's it.

181
00:07:24,361 --> 00:07:25,445
I am Maid of Honor.

182
00:07:25,486 --> 00:07:26,529
No, I am!

183
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:27,739
How come you are?

184
00:07:27,781 --> 00:07:30,825
Because I cared
enough to lie.

185
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:32,119
Hey, hey, hey.

186
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,703
I can help
you decide who
should do it.

187
00:07:33,745 --> 00:07:35,622
Yeah, we could have,
like, an audition

188
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:38,750
and see how you'd handle
Maid-of-Honor-type situations.

189
00:07:38,792 --> 00:07:40,085
What are you talking about?

190
00:07:40,127 --> 00:07:42,170
Like when I want a job,
I go to an audition.

191
00:07:42,212 --> 00:07:44,423
And if I'm the best
of the people they see

192
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:46,091
they give me the part.

193
00:07:46,133 --> 00:07:47,467
Okay, so after
this audition

194
00:07:47,508 --> 00:07:48,885
who decides
who gets it?

195
00:07:48,927 --> 00:07:51,138
Oh, uh, me and Ross
could be the judges.

196
00:07:51,179 --> 00:07:53,598
Well, it's better
than us deciding.

197
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:55,725
Oh, come on, this is crazy.
Can't we just flip a coin?

198
00:07:55,767 --> 00:07:58,561
No, coins hate me.

199
00:07:58,603 --> 00:07:59,854
Okay, fine.
You know what?

200
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:02,190
We will let Ross
and Joey decide.

201
00:08:02,232 --> 00:08:03,358
All right.

202
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,068
( seductively ):
Hi, Ross

203
00:08:05,110 --> 00:08:07,528
sweetie.

204
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:12,659
Hey, there, handsome thing.

205
00:08:16,121 --> 00:08:20,417
Wow, this cologne really is
every bit as good as Georgio.

206
00:08:26,714 --> 00:08:28,091
Hey.

207
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:31,386
Just, uh, brought back
your videos.

208
00:08:31,428 --> 00:08:35,515
Hey, uh, Ross, look, uh, I think
we need to talk about before.

209
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:37,976
No. No, we don't.

210
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:39,144
Yes, we do.

211
00:08:39,186 --> 00:08:40,437
Now, look

212
00:08:40,479 --> 00:08:42,939
that was the best nap
I ever had!

213
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:50,864
I don't, I don't know what
you're talking about.

214
00:08:50,905 --> 00:08:52,240
Come on. Admit it.

215
00:08:52,282 --> 00:08:54,909
That was the best nap
you ever had!

216
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:57,871
I've had better.

217
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:01,958
Okay. When?

218
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,710
All right, all right!

219
00:09:03,751 --> 00:09:05,920
It was the best nap ever!

220
00:09:05,962 --> 00:09:06,587
Uh-huh.

221
00:09:06,629 --> 00:09:07,672
I said it, okay!

222
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:09,924
But it's over, Joey!

223
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:13,428
I want to do it again.

224
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:19,434
We can't do it again.

225
00:09:19,476 --> 00:09:20,185
Why not?

226
00:09:20,227 --> 00:09:22,603
Because it's weird!

227
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:25,773
Fine.

228
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:27,401
You want something to drink?

229
00:09:27,442 --> 00:09:28,651
Sure, what do you got?

230
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:31,196
Warm milk and Excedrin P.M.

231
00:09:38,245 --> 00:09:39,620
Chandler.

232
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:42,957
Chandler, I just figured out
who you are.

233
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:46,711
Can you figure out
what I'm doing?

234
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:48,338
You're Louis Posin.

235
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:49,964
Who?

236
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:52,842
Louis Posin. He was
my best friend in fifth grade

237
00:09:52,884 --> 00:09:56,096
and then one day I asked him
to be my boyfriend

238
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:57,138
and he said no.

239
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,265
Do you know why?

240
00:09:58,306 --> 00:09:59,974
Because you kept talking
to him

241
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:02,394
while he was trying
to go to the bathroom?

242
00:10:02,436 --> 00:10:06,147
No, but because he thought I was
too "fa...aaaa..."

243
00:10:06,189 --> 00:10:08,066
And every time
I think about it

244
00:10:08,108 --> 00:10:11,027
it makes me feel as bad
as I did in fifth grade.

245
00:10:11,069 --> 00:10:13,488
You know, I really
think that you should

246
00:10:13,530 --> 00:10:14,739
apologize to Julie.

247
00:10:14,781 --> 00:10:16,450
Honey, are you kidding?

248
00:10:16,491 --> 00:10:17,992
That was, like,
16 years ago.

249
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:19,911
I know, but, you
know, it would make
me feel better

250
00:10:19,953 --> 00:10:21,204
if Louis apologized to me.

251
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:23,540
Okay, I will do it,
but I have to warn you

252
00:10:23,582 --> 00:10:27,043
this may make me a better
person, and that is not the man

253
00:10:27,085 --> 00:10:28,462
you fell in love with.

254
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:32,215
All right, this is how
it's going to work.

255
00:10:32,257 --> 00:10:33,550
We're going to give you

256
00:10:33,592 --> 00:10:35,051
hypothetical Maid of
Honor situations

257
00:10:35,093 --> 00:10:37,095
and you'll be scored
on a scale of one to ten

258
00:10:37,137 --> 00:10:38,388
one being the highest.

259
00:10:38,430 --> 00:10:39,722
No, ten is the highest.

260
00:10:39,764 --> 00:10:41,015
Why is ten the highest?

261
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:42,517
Because it's the highest.

262
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:47,522
Okay, Rachel

263
00:10:47,564 --> 00:10:49,065
you're up first.

264
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:50,400
Situation #1.

265
00:10:50,442 --> 00:10:51,401
You're with Monica.

266
00:10:51,443 --> 00:10:53,570
The wedding is
about to start

267
00:10:53,612 --> 00:10:55,947
when Monica gets
cold feet. Go!

268
00:10:55,989 --> 00:10:58,283
I don't want
to marry Chandler!

269
00:10:58,325 --> 00:10:59,200
Okay, um...

270
00:10:59,242 --> 00:10:59,951
I've got
cold feet.

271
00:10:59,993 --> 00:11:01,119
It's going
to be okay.  

272
00:11:01,161 --> 00:11:02,703
One man the rest
of my life?

273
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:04,122
I don't know
if I can do it.

274
00:11:04,164 --> 00:11:06,082
This means I'll
never get to sleep
with Joey!

275
00:11:07,334 --> 00:11:12,380
Look, Monica,
getting cold feet is
very common, you know?

276
00:11:12,422 --> 00:11:16,134
It's just because
of all the anticipation.

277
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:20,972
And you just have to remember
that you love Chandler.

278
00:11:21,014 --> 00:11:22,765
And also, I ran out
on a wedding.

279
00:11:22,807 --> 00:11:26,102
You don't get
to keep the gifts.

280
00:11:26,144 --> 00:11:27,770
Very good.
Drawing on your
own experience.

281
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:28,938
Thanks, cool.

282
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:29,939
Okay, good.

283
00:11:29,981 --> 00:11:32,484
Yes, very nice, Rachel.

284
00:11:32,526 --> 00:11:33,943
Thank you, judges.

285
00:11:33,985 --> 00:11:35,153
Oh, kiss ass.

286
00:11:35,195 --> 00:11:36,196
Uh!

287
00:11:37,738 --> 00:11:38,739
Okay, Phoebe.

288
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:40,950
Yes, Your Honor.

289
00:11:40,992 --> 00:11:43,119
We're now in
the ceremony.

290
00:11:43,161 --> 00:11:45,372
Monica is about
to say "I do"

291
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:48,208
when her drunk uncle
starts yelling.

292
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:49,792
What do you do? Go!

293
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:52,420
When Monica was a little girl

294
00:11:52,462 --> 00:11:53,421
I remember that...

295
00:11:53,463 --> 00:11:54,464
( yells )

296
00:11:54,506 --> 00:11:57,133
Oh!

297
00:11:57,175 --> 00:11:58,717
Ow!

298
00:11:58,759 --> 00:12:00,512
Very good!

299
00:12:02,138 --> 00:12:04,057
Yes, excellent.
Perfect score.

300
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:05,099
Wait a minute.

301
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:06,184
She just made
a scene

302
00:12:06,226 --> 00:12:07,810
in the middle
of the ceremony.

303
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:10,355
Hey, you want
a little taste of Pheebs?

304
00:12:10,397 --> 00:12:12,023
It is time for you

305
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:15,151
to give your Maid
of Honor speech.

306
00:12:15,193 --> 00:12:16,861
Oh, wait a minute,
we haven't even prepa...

307
00:12:16,903 --> 00:12:17,654
Go!

308
00:12:17,696 --> 00:12:19,822
Okay, okay, um...

309
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:23,076
Webster's dictionary defines
marriage as a...

310
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:24,911
No, no, forget that!
That sucks!

311
00:12:24,952 --> 00:12:26,745
Okay, never mind. Forget it.

312
00:12:26,787 --> 00:12:28,498
Um, um, okay.

313
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:33,587
Uh, I met Monica when we were
just a couple of six-year-olds

314
00:12:33,628 --> 00:12:38,216
and, uh, became friends
with Chandler when he was 25...

315
00:12:38,258 --> 00:12:41,094
although he seemed
like a six-year-old.

316
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:42,929
Oh, that was nice.

317
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:46,558
Thank you. Thank you very much.

318
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:50,604
Um, I've known them separately
and I've known them together

319
00:12:50,645 --> 00:12:52,813
and to know them as a couple is

320
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:56,276
to know that you are
truly in the presence of love.

321
00:12:56,317 --> 00:13:00,405
So, I would like to raise
my glass to Monica and Chandler

322
00:13:00,447 --> 00:13:02,490
and the beautiful adventure

323
00:13:02,532 --> 00:13:05,368
they are about to embark upon
together.

324
00:13:05,410 --> 00:13:09,914
I can think of no two people
better prepared for the journey.

325
00:13:09,956 --> 00:13:13,209
Wow.

326
00:13:13,251 --> 00:13:14,377
Great speech.

327
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:15,920
Yeah, it really was.

328
00:13:15,962 --> 00:13:17,088
Oh, thanks.

329
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:18,923
Okay, Phoebe,
I guess you're next...

330
00:13:18,965 --> 00:13:19,924
although I really

331
00:13:19,966 --> 00:13:21,259
don't see the point.

332
00:13:21,301 --> 00:13:22,343
Yeah.

333
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:26,681
Okay.

334
00:13:26,723 --> 00:13:28,683
( clears throat )

335
00:13:28,725 --> 00:13:30,059
I can't believe that

336
00:13:30,101 --> 00:13:32,729
Monica and Chandler are
getting married.

337
00:13:32,771 --> 00:13:35,982
I remember talking about this
day with Rachel

338
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:38,943
while we were showering
together... naked.

339
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:48,077
And she's back
in the game!

340
00:13:56,711 --> 00:13:58,879
Julie, hi.

341
00:13:58,921 --> 00:14:00,047
Chandler Bing.

342
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:01,341
I, uh, guess you
remember me.

343
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:03,968
Hello, Skidmark.

344
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:07,263
It's a nickname.

345
00:14:07,305 --> 00:14:08,931
I'll explain later.

346
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:10,891
It's pretty clear.

347
00:14:13,186 --> 00:14:17,273
Uh, I owe you
a long-overdue apology.

348
00:14:17,315 --> 00:14:18,941
I never should've
broken up with you

349
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:20,985
because you were
overweight.

350
00:14:21,027 --> 00:14:23,697
That's why you broke up with me?

351
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:29,160
Y-y-you didn't know that?

352
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:33,414
Well, I guess
my work here is done.

353
00:14:37,836 --> 00:14:40,213
Well, first of all,
I would like to say

354
00:14:40,254 --> 00:14:42,799
that you both performed
very well, okay?

355
00:14:42,841 --> 00:14:45,051
You should be proud
of yourselves.

356
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:46,636
And I'd also like
to say

357
00:14:46,678 --> 00:14:49,806
that in this competition,
there are no losers...

358
00:14:49,848 --> 00:14:51,098
Well, except Rachel...

359
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,475
Damn it!

360
00:14:53,768 --> 00:14:55,603
Really? I won?

361
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:56,354
What?

362
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:57,355
I'm sorry, Rach.

363
00:14:57,397 --> 00:14:58,732
It was
really close.

364
00:14:58,773 --> 00:15:00,608
Well, then,
I demand a recount!

365
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:02,652
Actually it wasn't
that close.

366
00:15:02,694 --> 00:15:03,986
No! You know what?

367
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:05,572
No. Your thing was
so stupid anyway.

368
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:07,114
We're going to flip a coin.

369
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:08,408
( gasps )

370
00:15:08,449 --> 00:15:10,827
All right? Heads.

371
00:15:10,869 --> 00:15:12,036
Oh!

372
00:15:12,078 --> 00:15:14,831
The coins have
finally forgiven me.

373
00:15:14,873 --> 00:15:16,499
Well, you
know what?

374
00:15:16,541 --> 00:15:20,628
I hope Monica forgives you
after you throw her

375
00:15:20,670 --> 00:15:24,924
her vegetarian, voodoo,
goddess-circle-y shower.

376
00:15:24,965 --> 00:15:26,342
Rach, it's going
to be okay.

377
00:15:26,384 --> 00:15:29,387
You guys are the best.

378
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:33,015
Boy, I'll tell you

379
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:36,018
that judging stuff
took a lot out of me.

380
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,395
Yeah?

381
00:15:37,437 --> 00:15:39,856
Yeah, I was thinking about maybe
going upstairs

382
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:41,900
and taking a little nap
on my couch...

383
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:47,488
Wh-why would I care about that?

384
00:15:48,531 --> 00:15:49,490
No reason.

385
00:15:49,532 --> 00:15:52,201
I'm just saying that, uh...

386
00:15:52,243 --> 00:15:54,328
...that's where I'll be.

387
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:16,183
As bad as that went

388
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:17,644
I actually
enjoyed myself.

389
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:19,228
I think that I am going

390
00:16:19,270 --> 00:16:22,523
to apologize for all
the stupid things that I do.

391
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:24,983
Why don't you just
stop doing stupid things?

392
00:16:25,025 --> 00:16:27,069
Then you wouldn't
have to apologize.

393
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:29,656
I'd really love it
if I could do both.

394
00:16:31,950 --> 00:16:35,495
All right, I have to ask...

395
00:16:35,536 --> 00:16:36,913
What?

396
00:16:36,955 --> 00:16:39,290
Are you going
to break up with me

397
00:16:39,332 --> 00:16:40,750
if I get fat again?

398
00:16:40,792 --> 00:16:42,084
What?

399
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:43,628
You broke up with
Julie Graff.

400
00:16:43,670 --> 00:16:45,588
How much weight
could she have gained?

401
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:48,132
145 pounds.

402
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:50,593
In one year?

403
00:16:50,635 --> 00:16:53,304
My God, what did she
eat, her family?

404
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:57,433
That's not the point.

405
00:16:57,475 --> 00:16:59,268
Look, I know it was
a stupid reason

406
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:01,604
to break up with somebody,
but I was 15.

407
00:17:02,981 --> 00:17:06,024
That's not the only time
this was an issue.

408
00:17:06,066 --> 00:17:10,279
You remember when you spent
Thanksgiving with us?

409
00:17:10,321 --> 00:17:11,906
You called me fat.

410
00:17:11,948 --> 00:17:13,574
Okay, okay, now, wait a minute.

411
00:17:13,616 --> 00:17:15,117
That was totally different.

412
00:17:15,159 --> 00:17:16,452
How?

413
00:17:16,494 --> 00:17:18,245
You were not supposed
to hear that.

414
00:17:18,287 --> 00:17:20,122
I said that behind your back.

415
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:22,000
What if I have babies, okay?

416
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:24,377
I mean, I'm going
to look different.

417
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:27,630
I'm okay with that,
but I'm not sure
that you are.

418
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:29,215
You have to realize

419
00:17:29,256 --> 00:17:31,091
I don't think of you
as a thin, beautiful woman.

420
00:17:35,722 --> 00:17:39,350
See, this is one of the things
that I can apologize for later.

421
00:17:39,392 --> 00:17:43,479
What I mean is,
you're Monica, okay

422
00:17:43,521 --> 00:17:46,733
and I am in love with Monica.

423
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:49,777
Keep going.

424
00:17:49,819 --> 00:17:53,031
So you can balloon up
or you can shrink down

425
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:55,033
and I will still love you.

426
00:17:55,073 --> 00:18:00,162
Even if I shrink down
to two inches tall?

427
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:02,957
I'd carry you around
in my pocket.

428
00:18:04,417 --> 00:18:05,501
I love you.

429
00:18:07,962 --> 00:18:11,799
Skidmark's still got
a way with the ladies.

430
00:18:13,885 --> 00:18:15,845
Hi, Pheebs.

431
00:18:15,887 --> 00:18:16,846
Hi.

432
00:18:16,888 --> 00:18:18,138
Hi.

433
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,390
I just want
to apologize.

434
00:18:19,432 --> 00:18:21,976
I'm really sorry
I was a baby.

435
00:18:22,018 --> 00:18:23,895
That's ridiculous, Rachel.

436
00:18:23,937 --> 00:18:25,730
We were all babies once.

437
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:30,526
Oh, you mean today.

438
00:18:30,568 --> 00:18:33,195
Yeah, and you know,
you deserve to win.

439
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:35,907
And, you know, I was
thinking about it--

440
00:18:35,949 --> 00:18:38,117
if you're Monica's
Maid of Honor

441
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:40,453
that means that
I get to be yours.

442
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:41,788
Oh, yeah!
Yeah.

443
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:45,083
Oh, um, when Monica
and Chandler got engaged

444
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:47,961
I started putting some
stuff together

445
00:18:48,002 --> 00:18:49,837
you know, just in case.

446
00:18:49,879 --> 00:18:51,589
Oh, that's so sweet. Thanks.

447
00:18:51,631 --> 00:18:55,093
Here is a book of poetry
that I know Monica loves.

448
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:56,385
And, uh, oh, God

449
00:18:56,427 --> 00:18:57,637
this is funny.

450
00:18:57,678 --> 00:18:59,973
Look, here's a picture
from one Halloween

451
00:19:00,014 --> 00:19:01,849
where she dressed up
as a bride.

452
00:19:01,891 --> 00:19:04,018
And look, she made me
carry her train

453
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:06,646
which was weird, because
I was Wonder Woman.

454
00:19:07,688 --> 00:19:09,065
Oh, and here's
a little purse

455
00:19:09,107 --> 00:19:10,942
that I found.

456
00:19:10,984 --> 00:19:14,112
You know, I just thought
they could maybe hold
the rings in there.

457
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:15,279
Oh, yeah.

458
00:19:15,321 --> 00:19:16,990
And, um,
here are some

459
00:19:17,031 --> 00:19:19,283
vintage handkerchiefs,
you know

460
00:19:19,325 --> 00:19:21,535
because people cry
at weddings.

461
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:26,124
( voice breaking ):
I'm just going to grab
a couple of these.

462
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:27,917
This stuff is great.

463
00:19:27,959 --> 00:19:29,919
Oh, I forgot this
was in here.

464
00:19:31,378 --> 00:19:35,591
Um, this was the garter
that I was saving

465
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:37,426
for my wedding...

466
00:19:37,468 --> 00:19:41,179
And I wanted it to be Monica's
something borrowed...

467
00:19:41,221 --> 00:19:42,515
And it's blue...

468
00:19:47,353 --> 00:19:50,272
You know, Rach, I think
that you should be

469
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:51,941
Monica's Maid of Honor.

470
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:55,611
You do?

471
00:19:55,653 --> 00:19:57,030
Why?

472
00:19:57,071 --> 00:20:00,198
Because I think it
means more to you.

473
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:02,952
But Pheebs, you know,
you earned it.

474
00:20:02,994 --> 00:20:04,162
It's fine.

475
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:05,663
I mean, this is
something

476
00:20:05,705 --> 00:20:07,581
that you've been
thinking about

477
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,167
since you were, what, 14?

478
00:20:09,207 --> 00:20:10,459
No, I was ten.

479
00:20:10,501 --> 00:20:12,545
I just developed early.

480
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:15,173
Man alive!

481
00:20:17,508 --> 00:20:18,801
Hey, what's going on?

482
00:20:18,843 --> 00:20:19,969
Hey!

483
00:20:20,011 --> 00:20:21,512
Well, we just decided
that Rachel

484
00:20:21,554 --> 00:20:23,181
is going to be
your Maid of Honor.

485
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:25,850
Oh, that's great!

486
00:20:26,893 --> 00:20:29,353
Oh, wow, okay, we really
have to start planning.

487
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:31,313
I have a lot of really
specific ideas.

488
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:34,108
We should probably
get together, like,
four times a week.

489
00:20:34,150 --> 00:20:35,776
You can come over
to my place.

490
00:20:35,818 --> 00:20:37,695
We'll get together
before work...

491
00:20:37,737 --> 00:20:39,822
What do you say,
6:30, my place?

492
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:41,157
So excited!

493
00:20:48,998 --> 00:20:51,167
Yeah, okay, you laugh now...

494
00:20:51,209 --> 00:20:53,127
She's going to be yours.

495
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:08,559
( sniffing )

496
00:21:09,602 --> 00:21:11,187
Mm, great nap.

497
00:21:11,229 --> 00:21:13,313
It really was.

498
00:21:13,355 --> 00:21:14,356
( clears throat )

499
00:21:31,457 --> 00:21:33,500
Dude, what the hell
are you doing?!

500
00:21:33,542 --> 00:21:35,293
God...!

501
00:21:41,884 --> 00:21:43,302
Excuse me.

